<title>GERMANY: RWE slams plan to shut Biblis nuclear plant.</title>
<headline>RWE slams plan to shut Biblis nuclear plant.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>German power company RWE Energie said on Friday the plan by the environment minister of the state of Hesse to close Biblis, Germany's oldest nuclear plant, was evidence of the nuclear authority's duplicity.</p>
<p>&quot;On the one hand the so-called security lapses at the plant are constantly denounced, while on the other hand state officials have blocked every attempt to improve the security at Block A of the plant,&quot; said the group, a unit of the giant RWE utility.</p>
<p>Earlier, Hesse's environment minister, Margarethe Nimsch, said she planned to withdraw the operating licence for Biblis.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
